     A          R HDLIST
     A                                  1  2'Help - Documents'
     A                                      DSPATR(HI)
     A                                  3  3'Each card is one of your documents-
     A                                      , ten to a page.  A document holds'
     A                                  4  3'up to 500 lines of text.'
     A                                  6  3'Type an option in the small field -
     A                                      at the top left of a card:'
     A                                  7  3'2 opens the editor, 6 prints the d-
     A                                      ocument, 4 deletes it.'
     A                                  8  3'Or put the cursor anywhere on a ca-
     A                                      rd and press Enter to open it.'
     A                                 10  3'F6 creates a new document.'
     A                                 11  3'F7 and F8 page backward and forwar-
     A                                      d through a long list.'
     A                                 23  2'Press Enter to return.'
     A                                      COLOR(BLU)
     A          R HDNEW
     A                                  1  2'Help - New document'
     A                                      DSPATR(HI)
     A                                  3  3'Give the document a short name and-
     A                                       a title, then press Enter.'
     A                                  4  3'The editor opens straight away.'
     A                                 23  2'Press Enter to return.'
     A                                      COLOR(BLU)
     A          R HDEDIT
     A                                  1  2'Help - Document editor'
     A                                      DSPATR(HI)
     A                                  3  3'Type on any of the fifteen lines. -
     A                                       What you type is kept when you pre-
     A                                      ss'
     A                                  4  3'Enter or any function key, but it -
     A                                      is only stored when you press F10.'
     A                                  6  3'F7 and F8 move up and down through-
     A                                       the document, fifteen lines at a t-
     A                                      ime.'
     A                                  7  3'F6 inserts an empty line where the-
     A                                       cursor is.'
     A                                  8  3'F9 deletes the line where the curs-
     A                                      or is.'
     A                                  9  3'F10 saves the document.  F11 print-
     A                                      s it.'
     A                                 11  3'F3 leaves.  If there are unsaved c-
     A                                      hanges you are warned once first.'
     A                                 23  2'Press Enter to return.'
     A                                      COLOR(BLU)
